{"kind":"assert","text":"M8 scope addendum: implicit capability workspace requirements and actual hook observation\n\nBaseline: clean de69ad3e012a0463c849662b2623e69681bf0656. Before editing:\npackages/derive/src/capability.ts 45ca159cb9496fda7ec8db3d197d11202b654fbc665def13ae112963df7be9e3\npackages/derive/src/effects.ts 16db2fd587f91d79cc962dfe0423edea3f4aeb0d399a6e093e51dc431bd77cee\npackages/derive/src/program/body.ts eb84d4203729362ab7f6952c0bc281bec7cf4dabe91a487b4bf60accadaad7b1\npackages/derive/src/program/observe.ts b6646ef2a1b2914bcaa95f02805e7ee000353da30c172d4d0c5d0dfb02ca0a9a\npackages/derive/src/program/requirements.ts 8be72141689e77d0a98fc1122e6325cc2c028c23a61d2128831dd7658ff2d8cc\npackages/derive/test/program-interpretations.test.ts e23f3fff048a5deb4ee2cc2f1d12b17fce62450b36a2d3699f2e323279e8863a\npackages/derive/test/forms-capability.test.ts 739f656f9cadfc8f5d4bb5600a25cdc779094e4cf1ff786437099cca760ef7b2\n\nThe shared effect leaf calls capabilities.workspace after declared effects and implicit hold endings. This callback can run without an explicit capability instruction. Requirements currently reports explicit capability interiors but misses that implicit workspace. Add its unknown requirement, the known hold scan/current-state requirements and the existing implicit identity/bounds inputs.\n\nObserve the existing guard, effect, deriveEffect and workspace interpreter hooks at their actual call sites. Each wrapper invokes its existing method exactly once, preserves receiver/arguments/order and records only hook metadata and completion. Never inspect opaque returned values or callback code. Scope the body observation to its actual admitted root so implicit callbacks retain their correct body. Availability checks and capability implementations stay in their existing homes.\n\nAdd one meaningful scripted hold-ending case to the current interpretation owner: a final transition ends an existing hold, invokes workspace once, preserves the full literal Ran across trace budgets, reports its opaque static requirement and restores observation after a callback fault. Strengthen the existing capability version-retention cases with captured judgments and exact hook counts across budgets. Preserve every earlier assertion, case and deadline, and change no shared fixture infrastructure.\n\nNo scope or replay source, accepted definition vocabulary, authority, wire format, pin, profile, scheduling policy or application callback implementation changes. The named first-slice and timed-array witnesses remain unchanged pending their planner rulings. Run the owning complete witnesses and narrow missing-workspace/duplicate-call controls under one frozen validation plan. Final assets, seals, gate, workflow and independent review remain ahead.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}